"toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{R}{R}","name":"Volcanic Fallout","oracle_id":"bd6ce147-c991-40ac-b276-65b630fad8b6","oracle_text":"This spell can't be countered.\nVolcanic Fallout deals 2 damage to each creature and each player.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-11-20","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.","oracle_id":"67c4b1d5-757c-46cf-8bb1-9889d9ed1a1f","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Slaughter Pact is countered or otherwise doesn't resolve (perhaps because its target became illegal), the delayed triggered ability that threatens you with a game loss won't trigger at the beginning of your next upkeep.","oracle_id":"67c4b1d5-757c-46cf-8bb1-9889d9ed1a1f","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Slaughter Pact resolves with a legal target but the target is not destroyed (perhaps because it has indestructible or regenerated), the delayed triggered ability will still trigger at the beginning of your next upkeep and you will have to pay the cost or lose the game.","oracle_id":"67c4b1d5-757c-46cf-8bb1-9889d9ed1a1f","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.","oracle_id":"782dcbc4-5a11-42f5-b8d9-4572e36d45b3","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Summoner's Pact is countered, the delayed triggered ability that threatens you with a game loss won't trigger at the beginning of your next upkeep.","oracle_id":"782dcbc4-5a11-42f5-b8d9-4572e36d45b3","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The delayed triggered ability will trigger regardless of whether any damage is actually prevented.","oracle_id":"9f9882f5-2338-4881-b418-b15348a462b4","published_at":"2007-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can’t be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.","oracle_id":"9f9882f5-2338-4881-b418-b15348a462b4","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Volcanic Fallout can be targeted by spells that try to counter it (such as Countersquall). Those spells will still resolve, but the part of their effect that would counter Volcanic Fallout won't do anything. Any other effects those spells have will work as normal.","oracle_id":"bd6ce147-c991-40ac-b276-65b630fad8b6","published_at":"2009-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.","oracle_id":"cf4959bf-92ae-4c9b-b631-724ce100cbb8","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Pact of the Titan is countered, the delayed triggered ability that threatens you with a game loss won't trigger at the beginning of your next upkeep.","oracle_id":"cf4959bf-92ae-4c9b-b631-724ce100cbb8","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You have to pay Pact of the Titan's cost during your next upkeep even if the Giant token doesn't survive that long. Okay, you don't have to, but it's a fairly good idea.","oracle_id":"cf4959bf-92ae-4c9b-b631-724ce100cbb8","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.","oracle_id":"f3e213a4-ba5a-468a-93b3-c0a34e1bd725","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Pact of Negation is countered or otherwise doesn't resolve (perhaps because its target became illegal), the delayed triggered ability that threatens you with a game loss won't trigger at the beginning of your next upkeep.","oracle_id":"f3e213a4-ba5a-468a-93b3-c0a34e1bd725","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Pact of Negation resolves with a legal target but fails to counter that spell (most likely because that spell can't be countered), the delayed triggered ability will still trigger at the beginning of your next upkeep and you will have to pay. Or else.","oracle_id":"f3e213a4-ba5a-468a-93b3-c0a34e1bd725","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
